- [x] ISC-4: Discord frontend live -- category per project, channel per agent, each agent replies under its own name and avatar via per-channel webhooks. Live-connected to "NW Life OS" server.
- [x] ISC-5: `/autopilot` per channel with "Always (this tool)" button; destructive/outbound actions still confirm regardless.
- [x] ISC-6: Phase 3a channel-aware delegation -- CoS delegates via `delegate` MCP tool; target agent runs in its own channel as its own task and reports back. Verified headless.
- [ ] ISC-7: Persistent memory -- per-channel SDK session resume (`resume`/`continue` + stored `session_id`) so a thread remembers prior messages across tasks.
- [ ] ISC-8: Gated `memory.md` updates -- agent can propose and apply updates to its own `memory.md` behind an approval gate.
- [ ] ISC-9: `ask_user` MCP tool -- agent posts a question to its channel and blocks until the next reply resolves it (mirror `pendingApprovals` pattern in `discordApp.ts`).
- [ ] ISC-10: qa-verify signs off on Phase 3 with PASS/FAIL evidence per criterion (typecheck + smoke test + live Discord check).
- [ ] ISC-11: Anti: no `@anthropic-ai/sdk` imported directly anywhere in `code/src/` (all AI calls through `Inference.ts` or Agent SDK).
- [ ] ISC-12: Anti: no committed secrets (`DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN`, `DISCORD_GUILD_ID`, Slack tokens) in `code/` or project root.
- [ ] ISC-13: Tokens rotated/revoked if still in a compromised state from prior paste-into-chat incident (flagged in `HANDOFF.md`).

